#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"Same semantics as the common :func:`tilelang.language.copy_op.copy`; the "
"extra keywords steer how the CUDA backend lowers the copy. They are "
"performance hints recorded on the tile op: compiling the same kernel for a "
"target that has no use for them leaves the result unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:33
msgid "Source memory region (Buffer, BufferLoad or BufferRegion)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:34
msgid "Destination memory region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:35
msgid "Width for coalesced memory access. Defaults to None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:38
msgid ""
"Never lower this copy through TMA even when the shape and scopes qualify. "
"Defaults to False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:41
msgid ""
"L2 cache eviction priority for the generated load/store or TMA instruction, "
"one of ``\"evict_normal\"``, ``\"evict_first\"``, ``\"evict_last\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"Preferred lowering instruction category: ``\"tma\"``, ``\"cp_async\"`` or "
"``\"sync\"``. For ``\"tma\"``, T.copy keeps synchronous copy semantics; "
"global -> shared copies lower through TMA with an automatically allocated "
"barrier and wait when constraints are satisfied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:51
msgid ""
"Additional annotations dict; values in it take precedence over the "
"individual keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/copy_op/index.rst:54
msgid "Parallel loop layout hint for the SIMT copy path."
msgstr ""

